  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Certonardosterol D3 and HepG2 through a series of target interactions. Certonardosterol D3 is identified as a target of two distinct compounds: MIP and Sophoradiol, with both of these compounds having HepG2 as their target. Similarly, Certonardosterol D3 is also a target of another compound, 2-(2,6-Dihydroxyphenyl)-5-hydroxy-3,6,7-trimethoxychromen-4-one, which also targets HepG2. These findings indicate that Certonardosterol D3 may play a role in modulating the activity of these compounds, which in turn affect HepG2 cells. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with varying degrees of support from different compounds. The evidence highlights a possible pathway where Certonardosterol D3 could influence the biological activity of other molecules, ultimately impacting HepG2. However, the exact mechanism by which Certonardosterol D3 interacts with these targets remains to be fully elucidated.",
